CZLite v0.3.8 kernel source distribution

The Linux kernel as a whole, including the integrated CZLite kernel changes,
is distributed under version 2 of the GNU General Public License. See
linux/COPYING and the complete text in linux/LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0.
The Linux-syscall-note exception applies to the user-space API as described
in linux/LICENSES/exceptions/Linux-syscall-note.

Individual upstream files retain their license notices and alternatives.
For example, the BMI270 driver offers GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause.
The M5Stack board sources retain bsp/COPYING and their per-file notices.
The license texts referenced by the BSP are provided in linux/LICENSES/.

The standalone CZLite build.sh, panel/generate.py, top-level .gitignore and
README.md are available under the MIT License in LICENSE-MIT. The same
license applies to the CZLite source export script in the originating SDK.
The kernel configuration records build settings from the released kernel.

Panel data provenance
The DCS command data in panel/cardputerzero.splash reproduces the settings
in M5Stack's modules/st7789v-1.0/cardputerzero,st7789v_lcd.bin at revision
4f7aeee9fc103ebb03d22cac476bb191ecfb321e. The 93-byte file in
linux/cm0-firmware/ matches that upstream file byte for byte. This release
carries the M5Stack repository-level terms in bsp/COPYING for the panel
initialization data in both representations. The upstream notice specifies
GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note. The standalone generator uses LICENSE-MIT.

Firmware image and userspace
The image contains software and peripheral firmware under multiple licenses.
Package versions and license notices are included in the source supplement
distributed with the release and in /usr/share/licenses/czlite/ on the device.
They include the Wi-Fi firmware notices, the Raspberry Pi boot firmware terms
and the Bosch BSD-3-Clause notice for the BMI270 configuration data.
